ng the  province to finally put in restrictions  that doctors have been calling for  for months here's eric sorensen  restrictions are all around us  the shuttered storefronts people masked  and not gathering in groups  workplaces with safe distances all the  measures so far  have not been enough the sick continue  to come in or be brought into hospitals  many health centers bursting at the  seams we've never seen ice use this  packed  and and the trajectory is still going up  so the province is now bringing in yet  more measures the emergency stay-at-home  order is being extended now to six weeks  outdoor gatherings limited to families  only an exception for people who live  alone  and checkpoints at all interprovincial  borders as well  non-essential construction sites will  close capacity and big box retail will  be reduced  churches will be down to 10 people  inside only  and new restrictions on golf and outdoor  recreation  ontario's premier says simply the covet  variants are winning the battle  the pace of our vaccine supply  has not kept up with the spread of the  new coved variants  we are on our heels but if we dig  in remain steadfast  we can turn this around the picture  grows more dire  the number of people in ontario  hospitals with covid virus or variants  is now approaching 2000  ontarians in intensive care now total  over 700  an unheard of number and yet the  projections show icu cases will rise to  800  soon and whether moderate measures or  new stronger measures  icu cases are expected to top a thousand  and go as high as 1500 next month  before leveling off for you know the  next week or two those numbers are baked  in that's not going to change that's the  nature of the disease  ontario has put out requests for nurses  from other provinces  alberta and saskatchewan have both said  they just can't spare any  so we just don't have the the capacity  to  start even talking about loaning  our health care workers out for a period  of time to other pr