ce of community  transmission but cases are expected to  rise  the capital was put under strict  lockdown yesterday when the city's first  infection was confirmed  all schools non-essential businesses and  government offices  are closed a deadly confrontation  between  police and a teenager coming up the  killing of a boy that's reigniting  demands  for police reform  a gunman who opened fire at a fedex  facility in indianapolis killed eight  people  and wounded several others the shooter  then took his own life at the scene  and tonight investigators aren't clear  on the motive  there was no confrontation with anyone  that was there there was no disturbance  there was no argument  he just appeared to randomly start  shooting  it happened late last night the gunman  opened fire in the parking lot before  entering the building  the shooting was over in a matter of  minutes police say the 19-year-old  suspect was a former employee  at the facility we're learning more  tonight about a deadly shooting  in chicago and a warning the details and  video in this next story  are disturbing police body cam footage  shows a 13-year-old boy with his hands  in the air  an officer then fires a shot and kills  the teen  this latest case comes as the u.s is  still reeling from another fatal  shooting at the hands of police  in minnesota and as jackson proskow  explains both  incidents are leading to calls to  rethink police training  19 seconds after responding to a report  of shots fired  the officer encountered 13 year old adam  toledo  that single gunshot to the chest was  fatal  another camera angle appears to show  toledo put his hands behind a fence  before turning towards the officer  police released this image which they  say shows the teen  was carrying a gun a weapon can be seen  on the ground in body camera footage  the family lawyer says the teen's hands  were up and empty when he was shot  that child was given a directive he  complied  he surrendered he turned to the of