n and frank's family members are  stricken by grief and bewilderment  maybe nothing could have saved anybody  in that immediate area  but to sleep six hours later  you know 30 minutes away wake up dude  all over again it's  that's how how  how can that happen rcmp say the gunman  slipped past them  and drove out of port-a-pick in his  mocked up rcmp vehicle  by using a different road than the one  they were guarding  but other information such as why an  emergency alert was never issued  remains murky after a series of erratic  news conferences  the rcmp promised more details from  their investigation  we commit to providing timely and  accurate updates  in the coming days and weeks that  promise 10 months ago  was the last time investigators faced  questions from the media  in a public setting the federal and nova  scotia governments have established a  public inquiry  headed by a mass casualty commission the  commission has been assigned to  investigate a wide range of questions  including  why the massacre happened and how police  responded  the commission says its final report due  in november of next year  will include recommendations for  preventing anything similar from  happening again  for families who were forced to protest  in the streets for a full public inquiry  trusting the process is a big leap of  faith they want more information  including details of the alleged role of  the gunman's common law partner lisa  banfield  in supplying him with ammunition police  say banfield and two others facing  charges had no prior knowledge of the  killer's plan  my trust in the inquiry and my trust in  the rcmp as a whole there's  there's none they wonder what has  changed  there are new measures including a ban  on assault rifles  on the sale of decommissioned police  vehicles and restrictions on used  uniforms  but other measures haven't happened  including a buy back on military-style  assault weapons  and reducing the smuggling of firearms  across the canada u